      "content": "Predictable flickering, like it happens at the exact same time every day, is certainly unusual, and it might suggest something more specific than a random electrical hiccup. It could be related to a cyclical load on the local grid, perhaps a surge coinciding with peak usage times, or maybe even an issue with the timer or sensor controlling that particular lamp. It's not uncommon for electrical faults to have patterns, though I can't say for sure without an electrician looking at it. It's a detail worth mentioning when you report it to the council!",
